## CHANGE 2 — Generate migration and wire up existing DB rows

Run: dotnet ef migrations add AddLessonIdToChallenge

Then READ the generated migration file. It will add a nullable LessonId column. After it is generated, EDIT it to add a SQL data-fixup that wires the existing seeded rows by matching OrderNumber within the zone.

Add this to the Up() method AFTER the AddColumn call:
```csharp
// Wire existing seeded challenges to their paired lessons by matching OrderNumber within the zone.
// This runs once on existing databases that were seeded before this migration.
migrationBuilder.Sql(@"
    UPDATE \"Challenges\" c
    SET \"LessonId\" = l.\"Id\"
    FROM \"Lessons\" l
    WHERE l.\"ZoneId\" = c.\"ZoneId\"
      AND l.\"OrderNumber\" = c.\"OrderNumber\"
");
```

Then run: dotnet ef database update

Verify the migration applied: the Challenges table should have LessonId populated for all 3 existing monsters.

